# OPUS GUBERNATIO PARTICIPANT PACKAGE og-participant-2026.08-v18
#
# SUCCESSOR to og-participant-2026.08-v17, whose checksum record is preserved unchanged at
# code_audit/run48_participant_package_v17_checksums.sha256 and is pinned to the commit whose
# blobs it describes, 5838a23. This record describes the LIVE TREE.
#
# RUN 49, THE COMPLETION OF THE NAMING CORRECTION. THREE of the seventy files moved, and TWO
# OF THE THREE ARE SEQUENCE-BEARING. That is stated first because it is what a reader most needs to know, and
# both exceptions are declared by name in server/tools/participant_packages.py rather than left
# for a checksum to discover.
#
# assets/js/deepdive.js -- SEQUENCE-BEARING, moved on the owner's ruling 1 of 2026-08-22. What
# moved inside it, exactly: the ten collapsible group headers drop the "Cat N" identifier span
# and render the group name alone; the Signal Stack banner, the Dempster-Shafer metric-box
# label, the synthesis comparison heading, its note and its three confidence sentences name what
# a module DOES rather than naming it by number; the comparison table drops the "Module NN"
# prefix from every row and the "Agrees with M09" column header; the Portfolio Health flyout
# drops the "D1.N" identifier from each module heading; and the panel label map is EXTENDED from
# nineteen keys to all seventy-seven keys the call sites actually pass, so each panel names its
# own category's purpose instead of collapsing onto one neutral phrase. CAT_NUM_FROM_MODULE, the
# grouping map, WAS NOT TOUCHED, so no panel moved to a different collapsible group.
#
# assets/js/decision-ui.js -- SEQUENCE-BEARING, moved on the owner's ruling 4 of 2026-08-22.
# COMMENTS ONLY, at the three inert "period: 1" literals, recording that the server derives the
# period from the research assignment and ignores the value. Not one byte of executable text in
# that file changed, and the file's behaviour was re-executed and is unchanged.
#
# assets/js/detail.js -- NOT sequence-bearing. One section title loses the ampersand the
# authority bars in user-facing text, and the executive brief prompt stops naming the retired
# scheme to the model while still forbidding the model to print any identifier.
#
# No step of the decision sequence, no reveal gate, no lock, no randomization, no server
# contract, no append-only record and NO USER-FACING CONTROL moved in any of the three.
# decision.js,
# workspace.js, intake.json and debrief.json are byte for byte identical to v17.
#
